  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Democratic Republic of Congo: Strengthening Professional Capacities for an Effective Anti-Corruption Response (SPC)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1)To ensure that DRC anti-corruption bodies endorse the need for a shared organizational framework for effective interagency operations. 2)To improve organizational and operational capacities of APLC and related bodies. 3)To improve the knowledge and practical skills of frontline APLC officers and related anti-corruption actors on the investigation, prosecution, and adjudication of corruption cases in line with national and international standards.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: APLC, OPJ, Inspection G&#xe9;n&#xe9;rale des Finances, Ministry of Justice, Ministry of Finance (including the Finance Intelligence Unit, the Cellule Nationale des Renseignements Financiers, the Central Bank of Congo, and financial institutions), Revenue Collection Agencies, Association of Congolese Banks, Financial Reporting Centre, and selected magistrates.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to ensure that l&apos;Agence de Pr&#xe9;vention et de Lutte contre la Corruption (APLC), Officiers de Police Judiciaire (OPJ) and selected magistrates conduct investigation, prosecution, and adjudication of crimes of corruption, money-laundering and terrorist financing in line with international standards.</narrative>
  </description>
